depgraph: skip the cycle closure pass when it cannot select anything (_GatherOkTracker)

When no leaf is available, find_smallest_cycle calls
_gather_deps_closures for each priority level: one O(V+E) pass over the
graph that computes, for every candidate, whether gather_deps succeeds and
how large its closure is. In most passes of the selection loop that work
selects nothing, because no candidate with parents is in the resulting
ok_nodes. _GatherOkTracker (one per priority range and level) maintains
exactly that ok_nodes set across passes: while the graph only loses nodes,
an ok node stays ok until removed, and a not-ok node stays so as long as
its recorded witness (a not-ok child) is still there, so only the nodes
whose witness chain was cut are re-examined. If nodes or edges were added,
or a node left the candidate set while staying in the graph, the set is
rebuilt from scratch by the same procedure. When the tracker's set holds no
candidate with parents, the closure pass is skipped for that level; when it
does, the original code runs unchanged and decides.

